  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better Farming in Northern Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Project overall objective is to accelerate the transition of Northern Ghana&#xbf;s agriculture sector towards sustainability, resilience and Food Security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project is structured around the three specific objectives:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Increase the productivity levels of agricultural production systems through the dissemination of climate-resilient agroecological practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Sustainable improvement in the income of women (and other vulnerable groups, including young people) through the development of processing (in particular small-scale processing of shea butter) and improved access to markets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Support for the implementation of Ghana&apos;s agricultural policy, in particular actions to promote agro-ecological transition and those relating to the regulation of the shea industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The activities implemented are organized into 3 main components which are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 1: Improved management of the shea nut resource&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 2: Support for the agro-ecological intensification of the soya, vegetables and beekeeping value chains&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Component 3: Institutional strengthening for the implementation of Ghana&apos;s agricultural policy&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is a 4th component for the project management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project interventions are located in the 5 regions of Northern Ghana (Savannah, Northern, Upper Est, Upper West, North West).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
